yamlover/code
description: One yamlover document's content - the project's own text language
- >
  **yamlover** is this project's own text language - a CLOSE KIN of YAML, deliberately NOT a
  superset (the [differences have their own chapter](*::language:vs-yaml)). Kept from YAML:
  block and flow spelling, comments, every scalar style. Extended with the POINTER LAYER -
  `*` references over colon paths, `&` bookmarks - and the UNIFIED NODE, where keyed
  entries, positions, and a scalar self-value mix freely:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  pets:
    - name: Rex
    - name: Whiskers
  feline: *pets: 1
  boss: &: chief
    name: Rex
  team:
    lead: *: chief
- >
  See the subchapters below for the parts; comments are exactly YAML's:
- *: 00-yamlover_structured
- *: 01-yamlover_scalar
- *..:..:..:04-yaml:01-yaml_code:02-yaml_comment
